  <p class=3D"corner-intro">A collection of web design and development news=
 and thoughts from CodePen's own Chris Coyier.</p>=0D=0A                   =
       </mj-raw>=0D=0A                          <p>In <a href=3D"https://go=
.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/AEXW8EXITRwxppFmjmqZJQ~~/AABEfhA~/PfM0aiB_DPt93B92=
pcTgF3O8Y09iUCuDd5UwFC9X74qxSXsHS5W3l6oBIwDtFEtqMZjhKnBEAfifFEbRGVumt1Jhqpj=
roBWZNazsaMZVFWXhHlGYDEvrOj16XYUim2_cF0RzqM2-vtzcdB-RgJZ3jqY-yd71hTdMxDsnxq=
Wqx71J2plnaqSx7X_yFp6v_Oxo">Fixing the URL params performance penalty</a>, =
Barry Pollard sets up a very clear real-world conundrum. The content at the=
se two URLs is probably the same:</p>=0A<ul>=0A<li><code>https://www.exampl=
e.com/</code></li>=0A<li><code>https://www.example.com/=3Futm_source=3Demai=
l</code></li>=0A</ul>=0A<p>The content at these two URLs is probably not:</=
p>=0A<ul>=0A<li><code>https://www.example.com/products=3Fproductid=3D1234</=
code></li>=0A<li><code>https://www.example.com/products=3Fproductid=3D5678<=
/code></li>=0A</ul>=0A<p>Who cares=3F Cache cares. Because content with dif=
ferent query params <em>might</em> be different, the various tech that deal=
s with caching has to <em>assume it will</em> be different. But that stinks=
 tho. And it=E2=80=99s not a new problem.</p>=0A<p>I=E2=80=99m not sure wha=
t the history or landscape of solutions is for this, but one from the Chrom=
e gang that is rolling out from them is a new header: <code>No-Vary-Search<=
/code>. The idea is that you get the control as the owner of the site to sa=
y how it works on your site.</p>=0A<pre><code class=3D"js">No-Vary-Search: =
params, except=3D(&quot;q&quot; &quot;productid&quot;)=0A</code></pre>=0A<p=
>So with a header like the above, you=E2=80=99re saying =E2=80=9Cquery para=
ms never matter on this site, they will not effect the content on the page,=
 except for these two, those two do.=E2=80=9D That seems awfully useful to =
me. Just don=E2=80=99t get it wrong.</p>=0A<p>Speaking of URLs, you know wh=
at site <s>used to have</s> has great URLs=3F Flickr, the photo sharing sit=
e. Why did that have to fade away, anyway=3F I think it was basically infin=
ite cloud storage of camera rolls on mobile phones and Instagram. I do hope=
 there is a resurgance of =E2=80=9Ca social place to share my best photos=
=E2=80=9D that does well again, but I digress. Flickr=E2=80=99s URLs were g=
reat, and Marcin Wichary sings their praises in <a href=3D"https://go.spark=
postmail2.com/f/a/w2Jmn34RcpR91EvXgSHFjg~~/AABEfhA~/600tH5QAC91VO7DYCVD5QPi=
uiDF8pZyS2tDbtHpbyxVPTYjUhDxzdt5Os2x15efVb63Y4Ii7P6sfLp2kFBYirMIoa9w_Z6PJB-=
CqS8iXOJex1f11x94LCAZyL2xU_qPsKedvthVVqlysdexW6FxuHMDtGG9w359n_0_jiRdYlUk~"=
>Unsung heroes: Flickr=E2=80=99s URLs scheme</a>.</p>=0A<pre><code class=3D=
"html">flickr.com/photos/mwichary/favorites =0Aflickr.com/photos/mwichary/s=
ets=0Aflickr.com/photos/mwichary/sets/72177720330077904=0Aflickr.com/photos=
/mwichary/54896695834=0Aflickr.com/photos/mwichary/54896695834/in/set-72177=
720330077904=0A</code></pre>=0A<blockquote><p>This was incredible and a bre=
ath of fresh air. No redundant <code>www.</code> in front or awkward <code>=
.php</code> at the end. No parameters with their unpleasant <code>=3F&=3D<=
/code> syntax. No <code>%</code> signs partying with hex codes. When you sh=
ared these URLs with others, you didn=E2=80=99t have to retouch or delete a=
nything. When Chrome=E2=80=99s address bar started autocompleting them, you=
 knew exactly where you were going.</p></blockquote>=0A<p>If you have found=
 yourself on Flickr recently, it might be because NASA is on Flickr and <a =
href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/YMhLNGfsb0UWHhOXm5EVzQ~~/AABEfhA~=
/NnhTk1NYQWuCqeCP5tzBU3B3Rk8W_Z16mqqv-yf8-LaB7eB50fmSB0VxFlCcavyZeL7l0IouuF=
2SVINYLcXoowJ4KF3WYK-Qwls0_wBcjVIeJKeRwdUrX1j5eDir_Gp2pTQrhNHuvLCgr-u-rUkA4=
g~~">the Artemis II mission posts their official photos</a> there. There=E2=
=80=99s some <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/_TnyVkvHTFXIU1EDv=
fi-CQ~~/AABEfhA~/7QioAjq06JJUAUEbroYhPOXi0ZmpE6-OkfrpU2gZUbP3alhtcLQ0Gqfb-M=
PoOvs_4uqrr9lmYStTS16Ab6HM1GXMlN_6v9pTr3t1qgFK1LnoMCviHaBTM-27GeSmE2wRMR3yA=
ogAp7cOho7sPT3qEgbmRx-z1PUpKsBAueMEdHydJS9agK5s8X6mDmxJ-8XPh1CVHqUVfiwud71i=
R1fQdQ~~">really great photos</a> there, still rocking those equally great =
URLs.</p>=0A<p>There are <em>new</em> ideas in clever URLs out there as wel=
l. You know how there are some unofficial but obvious conventions for certa=
in pages=3F I mean like the contact page is probably <code>/contact</code> =
and the page for hiring is probably <code>/hiring</code>. What is the URL f=
or changing your password=3F There is no real convention for that. It might=
 exist on a dedicated URL or it might be part of a settings or account page=
.</p>=0A<p>If there was a strong convention (and <a href=3D"https://go.spa=
rkpostmail2.com/f/a/KQElmFfXw1zdX375tJpl5w~~/AABEfhA~/X97hCwdbZvMlyXiqXDIux=
G70dEugliqLSvPhCNhxB4t7nWN21--JxMT5MwDWzTGHu104e5YNlmAcuAzJlY661-CMl3oA9yYT=
s9YekQHYXfFFYhIYwH1FW_sEcCUfKLE3k-fgEyoM51JW0xhv-vMCBuMHMtvXHWeqf0vlp8AN2Pq=
FardGSSajqMhv252ePscpGhCFRQt0Kwa9x0r1fuyXe5meQHKW1GBbr0CI8u8QKSJ9ILCov-YjE-=
_9_c2vXpjedSPMjlcavejKyXEK47DsjnQF-rfSgtCAecyCwLisKnM~">here=E2=80=99s Eiji=
 Kitamura suggesting just that</a>) users, and perhaps more importantly pas=
sword managers, would know how to get you there. The URL=3F</p>=0A<pre><cod=
e class=3D"html">/.well-known/change-password=0A</code></pre>=0A<p>I don=E2=
=80=99t know much about that special directory, I know it=E2=80=99s just us=
ed for things like verifying DNS setups and payment processors and stuff. S=
eems like a perfectly good usage for me. And it doesn=E2=80=99t mean <em>th=
at</em> URL is where you actually change your password, it just redirects t=
o wherever makes sense in your site.</p>=0A<p>Too weird to take off=3F Here=
=E2=80=99s some sites already doing it:</p>=0A<ul>=0A<li>Google</li>=0A<li>=
GitHub</li>=0A<li>Facebook</li>=0A<li>Twitter</li>=0A<li>WordPress</li>=0A<=
/ul>=0A<p>Cool.</p>=0D=0A                          =0D=0A                  =
